model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "A read's result that a server-rendered document carries reaches the browser as old as it was when the server sent it, on the browser's own clock: before any page code reads it, the browser adds the difference between its time on arrival and the server's time of sending to the time on the result's success, or on the earlier success a failure still holds. Freshness, which compares that time with the browser's clock, therefore does not depend on the two clocks agreeing. A browser whose clock is ahead of the server's reads no hydrated value again on a new document, and one whose clock is behind does not keep a value past its freshness. The 30 second freshness and every other read rule are unchanged. The time a document spends in transit is not counted, and documents are never served from a cache. Only a value that is itself a result is moved; a result nested in another value, such as a protected read's accepted body, keeps the server's time, and nothing judges that one's freshness by its time."
    }
  }
}
